  "result": "Here's a first draft. It's about 105 words, and I haven't added it to `README.md`.\n\n```markdown\n## Carriers\n\nEach carrier lives in its own module under `shop/carriers/` (for example, `shop/carriers/acme.py`). There are 20 of them, and each is registered by name in `REGISTRY` in `shop/carriers/__init__.py`. Use `shop.carriers.get(\"acme\")` to look one up.\n\nEvery carrier module defines a `BASE_RATE` in cents, a per-weight rate, a `ZONES` table of multipliers and a maximum weight. A quote is `(BASE_RATE + per-weight rate \u00d7 weight) \u00d7 zone factor`.\n\nAll carriers take weight in kilograms except **Maple** (`shop/carriers/maple.py`), which takes grams. It uses `PER_GRAMS` and `MAX_GRAMS` (30000) instead of `PER_KG` and `MAX_KG`, so pass Maple a weight in grams.\n```\n\nEach carrier file has a TODO saying its zone table still needs confirming with the carrier's account manager. You might want to mention that in the README too.",
